# Type annotations read like English: "A is a positive-definite N by N matrix
# of kilograms". A lone name is a unit (`N` is newtons, `K` kelvin), a name
# before a shape word is a matrix property, and a name inside `[...]` is a
# size variable.
t: s
v: Vector[3] m/s
A: PositiveDefinite Matrix[N, N]
K: Symmetric Diagonal Matrix[3, 3] N/m
x: Scalar
M: Tensor[B, T, D] kg
f: N
T2: K
w: Vector[3,] kg*m^2/s^2
h: m^(1/2)
B: Matrix[3, 4] = zeros(3, 4)
C: Symmetric Matrix[N, N] kg = A
a: m/s^2 = 9.8 m/s^2
